text: >-
  HealthRanger & @HealthRanger • 5h

  G ...

  I don't mean to be graphic, and I mean no disrespect to Charlie Kirk and his

  tragic assassination, but shouldn't we be asking why there doesn't appear

  to be an exit wound and blood splatter on the large white banner directly

  behind Charlie when he was shot? If the shot came from the roof with a

  front-facing shot, there would be unmistakable blood splatter directly

  behind Charlie. A 30-06 rifle round would have traveled all the way through

  the flesh and would have made a very large exit path, carrying blood and

  tissue with it. Again, apologies for being graphic, but I don't know any other

  way to ask this question. It's just that this is one more thing that isn't
  adding

  up. And like you, I just want answers. I want to know who did this.
